  "engineering_change_reason": "Version 3 uses off/low/medium because xhigh repeatedly failed to expose usable structured final content under budget-compatible ceilings. Study 1 is pinned to the zero-retention AkashML FP8 endpoint. Paid engineering traces showed that a 900-token low completion cap could still be fully consumed by low-effort reasoning on an outlier respondent, while reasoning-off responses repeatedly required about 68 tokens. Completion headroom was therefore reallocated without increasing total allowance: off 120, low 1100, medium 1430. These caps still sum to 2650 completion tokens per respondent and preserve the exact USD 7.745162 full-study provider-ceiling projection below the USD 7.80 Study 1 cap. No human truth was loaded for scoring and no predictive performance was inspected when making this engineering change.",
